          "path": "_m/g/c/v/p/cambuskenneth-abbey-wp/cambuskenneth-geograph-org-uk-.jpg",
          "filename": "Cambuskenneth - geograph.org.uk - 25774.jpg",
          "caption": "Cambuskenneth. Looking across the Forth to the near island of Cambuskenneth, grazing Herefords and the ruined abbey. Beyond the Ochil scarp, foreground is made of the dreadful giant hogweed, giant plants with a sap that blisters in sunlight. The meanders of the tidal Forth are plagued by this alien weed, a garden escapee.",
